            <ArticleTitle>NHC-catalyzed cleavage of vicinal diketones and triketones followed by insertion of enones and ynones.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1816-1822</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3762/bjoc.13.176</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thiazolium carbene-catalyzed reactions of 1,2-diketones and 1,2,3-triketones with enones and ynones have been investigated. The diketones gave α,β-double acylation products via unique Breslow intermediates isolable as acid salts, whereas the triketones formed stable adducts with the NHC instead of the coupling products.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
